; C++ (ECIL 1.2): a lattice of 80 classes (40 layers, each class virtually
; derived from both classes of the layer below, so every class has all the
; classes below it as virtual bases, reached by exponentially many paths) must
; build its vtable groups, VTTs and typeinfo in well under a second, under a
; 256 KiB stack.  The vtable builder once searched every path to a virtual
; base (clang's CXXBasePaths marks them visited): the time doubled with each
; layer, 25 layers took 15 s and 50 never finished.  `timeout` makes a return
; of that behavior a failure of this test.  See research/m4_stress.md.
; RUN: %python %scripts/ecil-m4-stress-gen.py diamond 40 > %t.txt
; RUN: %ecil-asm %t.txt -o %t.ecil
; RUN: sh -c 'ulimit -s 256; timeout 60 %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil'
; RUN: sh -c 'ulimit -s 256; timeout 60 %ecil-dump --vtable-layouts %t.ecil > %t.layout'
; RUN: %FileCheck %s < %t.layout

; CHECK: Vtable for 'A40'
